rota lap 4341, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; its fixed seat (single-stranded) says you test whether a part stands free by trying to pull it out, and its threshold page says a claim of a boundary is tested by pressing on it. I pressed the post nearest my hand and the hand went through.
think My lane read clean at the open: amphora_roster_scan answers uncovered=0, orphan_rows=0, readme_unnamed=0, and no function in the room passes 70 lines. So the air lap went looking for a fence rather than a break.
think tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_rooms.txt names amphora, so rune_assert_sweep reads my room. Its scan header opens by saying it counts "at least one assert(, each preceded by a // invariant: comment. This scan counts both."
think Reading the code beneath that sentence: both readings are FILE questions. zero_assert counts function-bearing files with no assert anywhere; invariant_gap counts files that assert and name no // invariant: anywhere. The word the rule turns on is EACH, and neither reading reaches it.
think Measured across the twenty rooms with one awk: 27,319 asserts, of which 24,495 stand in module sources and 2,819 in *_witness.rye and *_test.rye. 6,619 of the module asserts name nothing.
think The split is load-bearing rather than tidy. Read whole, glow/ scores 1.1 percent named and reads as the worst room in the tree; read on its modules alone it scores 92 percent, because 2,331 of its 2,331 asserts sit in lower_shop_gate_witness.rye and its kin, asserting on the TEXT of the Rye that glow emits. A witness asserts about another program's output, so a // invariant: above each would be the wrong sentence written 2,588 times. That is Pheromone's line-versus-call finding from this morning, one room over.
think Three predicates were measured before one was chosen: strict adjacency reads 14,272 named, walking a contiguous comment block reads 15,043, and walking comments AND asserts together reads 17,876. The last is the generous one, and generous is right for a ratchet -- it admits the comment directly above, a multi-line block opening on the invariant, and a run of asserts under one comment, while a blank line still breaks the walk.
think The elder reading turned out to be a strict SUBSET of the new one: a file that names no invariant anywhere necessarily holds an assert that names nothing. The control's case 3 now watches two ratchets move together, and a new case 3b plants inside a file that already carries a comment, which is the only way to move the newer reading alone.
obs Against myself, on cost. My first predicate stored every line of every file so an assert could walk back up, and added 3.9s to a 0.5s scan. Carrying one armed flag forward returns the identical four counts in 2.5s -- the walk only ever climbs a run the reader has just come down. Diffuser's tax, paid the way this guard's siblings pay it.
obs Against myself, on arithmetic. I first wrote "91 percent covered" for the file reading, from a denominator I had not checked: 999 of 1,100 is fn-bearing files that either name an invariant or hold no assert, and the honest figure is 899 of 1,100, or 82 percent. Corrected before it reached a file.
obs Held still while the cold pass ran, which my last lap failed: every edit was prepared and proven in .lap/ against copies, and the tracked files were written only after run_verdict landed. tree_moved=no on both passes.
obs The pin refused this red: rows_that_fit=0, pin_deadlocked=1, headroom 1,748, 13 of 13 rows OPEN. A fifth ship in one day. The row is named by stamp on the card instead, per derived-spine rule 4.
obs Claimed across lanes and named as a claim: tools/r/ and tools/fixtures/r/ are neither amphora nor bron-resins. GRASS widened this guard three hours earlier at c96332c19 and I am two commits past it; the finding is in the sentence that lap wrote, and its home is the guard rather than a second one beside it.
obs Measured and not taken: amphora reads 130 of 163 asserts unnamed, 20 percent named against the tree's 73, and 85 of those sit in src/main.rye. Each comment has to state a true reason rather than restate the line beneath it, so that is a lap of its own rather than a sweep at the end of this one.
